\subsection{Statistical robustness}\label{sec:robust}
\paragraph{EoS-level bootstrap.} The intervals of the preceding sections describe re-partitioning of the same 360 EoS. Table~\ref{tab:boot} instead gives 95\% intervals from resampling whole EoS within each class (2000 resamples; each EoS's predictions pooled over the three partitions). The noise-free accuracy of the MLP ensemble is @@bs_ALL_0_MLP-ens_acc@@\% [@@bs_ALL_0_MLP-ens_acc_lo@@, @@bs_ALL_0_MLP-ens_acc_hi@@], the recall of strange matter is 100\% [100, 100], and the accuracy between the nucleonic and dark-matter classes is @@bs_ALL_0_MLP-ens_pair@@\% [@@bs_ALL_0_MLP-ens_pair_lo@@, @@bs_ALL_0_MLP-ens_pair_hi@@]; with NICER-like errors and a 20\% $f$-mode it is @@bs_NICERpf20_MLP-ens_pair@@\% [@@bs_NICERpf20_MLP-ens_pair_lo@@, @@bs_NICERpf20_MLP-ens_pair_hi@@] and the overall accuracy @@bs_NICERpf20_MLP-ens_acc@@\% [@@bs_NICERpf20_MLP-ens_acc_lo@@, @@bs_NICERpf20_MLP-ens_acc_hi@@]. The intervals for the nucleonic--dark-matter pair contain 50\% in every scenario, so indistinguishability is not an artefact of a particular partition of this finite sample.
